        "original_id": "c4d20512-9d39-54bb-8c3c-bb3c49dd7826",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alma Wade\n- Products: F.E.A.R., SAS: Secure Tomorrow\n- Companies: Monolith Productions, Sierra Entertainment\n- Systems: Jupiter EX engine\n- Topics: survival horror, first-person shooter video games\n\nFacts:\n- Monolith Productions introduced Alma Wade in the 2005 video game F.E.A.R.\n- Alma Wade is a major antagonist and key figure in the F.E.A.R. series.\n- Alma Wade is described as the core mystery of the F.E.A.R. series.\n- F.E.A.R. First Encounter Assault Recon is a survival horror first-person shooter video game.\n- Monolith Productions developed F.E.A.R. First Encounter Assault Recon.\n- Sierra Entertainment published F.E.A.R. First Encounter Assault Recon.\n- SAS: Secure Tomorrow uses the Jupiter EX engine.\n- The Jupiter EX engine used in SAS: Secure Tomorrow is similar or possibly identical to the engine used in F.E.A.R.",
